# PART III — MODEL VERSION COMPLETION AND SELECTION

## S0. Complete branch requirement

A model branch is not complete when it has produced attractive sample sections.

It must contain:

- the full continuous essay;
- all eight station passes;
- completed local and whole-work reviews;
- source and status audits;
- comparative and negation ledger;
- admitted visuals;
- depth records needed to judge the version;
- link targets;
- run manifest;
- test results;
- a compact note on deliberate writing-law exceptions.

Every branch is judged at the same state of completion.

## S1. Cross-model comparison

Completed branches are compared without merging them first.

The comparison uses:

- conceptual fidelity;
- preservation of Frank’s proposition;
- section and whole-work flow;
- clarity of actors and operations;
- teaching before compression;
- source and register discipline;
- voice continuity;
- absence of machine cadence;
- quality of transitions;
- handling of richness;
- strength of ending and return;
- quality of depth relations;
- reader experience without links.

Model identity is not treated as evidence of quality.

The evaluator reads branch outputs in a neutral order. Where possible, branch labels are masked during the first prose comparison.

## S2. Frank’s selection

Frank decides:

- the primary manuscript branch;
- whether another branch contains a specific superior operation, paragraph, transition, figure, or depth record;
- which material is rejected;
- which questions remain open.

The final version should normally preserve one branch as its prose body.

It should not become a sentence-by-sentence collage of model outputs. Cross-branch imports occur only when the imported unit performs a clear operation the primary branch lacks. Every import triggers seam, voice, source, and rubric re-audit.

## S3. Integration branch

Create an integration branch after selection:

```text
codex/written-edition-final
```

This branch begins from the selected primary version.

It receives:

- Frank-approved imports;
- final source corrections;
- final figures;
- final depth records;
- final link and minigraph generation;
- public-vault projection;
- release metadata.

No worktrees are used. Integration is sequential and has one write owner at a time.

After full verification, the integration branch is merged into `main` or otherwise designated as the canonical written edition according to Frank’s repository decision.

